{
  "id": "zero_sum.mixed_matrix_payoff",
  "title": "Expected Payoff of a Matrix Game",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "formalized",
  "href": "zero_sum/zero_sum_mixed_matrix_payoff.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Expected Payoff of a Matrix Game</h1>\n<p>For mixed strategies $x \\in \\Delta(I)$ and $y \\in \\Delta(J)$, the expected\npayoff of the matrix game $A$ is</p>\n<p>$$E_A(x,y) = \\sum_{i \\in I}\\sum_{j \\in J} x_i y_j A(i,j).$$</p>\n<p>The one-sided forms $E_A(x,j)$ and $E_A(i,y)$ describe mixed play against a\npure response.</p>",
